    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d203">

                <pb facs="0277" n="263" xml:id="pg263"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.7962/12–2048: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Childs</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-12-20T15:00:00+03:00">December 20,
                            1948—3 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>655. Deptels 471 and 472<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d203-f1"/> most helpful. Although arguments outlined re Dhahran have
                    been generally used previously in my formal talks with Foreign Minister, I went
                    over ground again today with him although not referring to paragraph 7 SAG note January 2, 1946 inasmuch as it makes
                    operation airfield by SAG conditional upon its
                    not becoming a burden on Saudi Treasury.</p>
                <p>Yusuf stated he would await Department’s reaction proposals for renewal on basis
                    exchange of notes as submitted (see Legtels 648 and 651<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d203-f2"/>). I do not anticipate SAG
                    will offer any objections re affirmation outlined exchange notes mentioned but
                    as those notes form integral part existing Dhahran airbase agreement particular
                    advantages not perceived to single out certain provisions that agreement for
                    affirmation.</p>
                <p>Inasmuch as difficulties set forth by Dept in connection tripartite agreement
                    recognized previously by Legation, I have consistently endeavored throw as much
                    cold water on project as might be done without dampening Saudi spirits.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Childs</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
